{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Magnets: attract or repel?","theme":{"background":"#1e2a3a","foreground":"#ffffff","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Magnetic poles"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Every magnet has two ends called poles: a north pole and a south pole."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Attract or repel"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Attract means pull together. Repel means push apart. Unlike poles attract. Like poles repel."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Two north poles are brought close together. What happens?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"They attract","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"They repel","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Nothing happens","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"A north pole is brought near a south pole. What happens?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"They repel","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"They attract","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"They spin around","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"magnet"},{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Two south poles are brought close together. What happens?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"They attract","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"They stick together","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"They repel","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"Which pair of poles will attract each other?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"North and north","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"South and south","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-c","label":"North and south","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"Two magnets are placed with a north pole facing a north pole. What will they do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"Pull together","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Push apart","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-c","label":"Stay still","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"You find two bar magnets on the table. Which will you test first?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Turn one magnet around, then bring the poles together","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Put the two magnets side by side and watch","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"You turn one magnet around and bring the poles together. They push apart. You predicted it right!"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"end"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-t","content":"You watch the magnets side by side. They do not touch. Check the poles before you test again."},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"end"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"end","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"end-h","content":"Well done! You finished the magnet poles quiz."},{"type":"text","id":"end-m","content":"Remember: unlike poles attract and like poles repel. Keep testing and keep predicting!"}],"actions":[]}}
